<task id="010" project="messaging-communication-app-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>ACS identity + server-side chat-token minting (`communicationUserId ↔ Dataverse`; uniform minting)</title>
    <phase>W1 — ACS Integration (server-side only)</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>7</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>003, 005</dependencies>
    <blocks>011, 020, 051</blocks>
    <tags>bff-api, acs, auth</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Net-new BFF service under `Services/Communication/Acs/` that talks to an external Azure resource (ACS) and mints security tokens; touches auth (ADR-028 central credential), persists a new cross-entity identity mapping (`communicationUserId`), and is a hard prerequisite for all messaging transport (blocks 011/020/051). Tags include `bff-api` + `auth`; security-sensitive token surface; publish-size + CVE governance applies.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W1</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-03</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Build the **ACS identity plane** for the messaging channel, server-side only, in a NEW `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Acs/` folder. Two responsibilities:

    • **Identity creation + mapping** — the BFF (ACS "trusted service") creates an ACS identity (`CommunicationIdentityClient.CreateUser`) for any Spaarke participant that lacks one, and persists the resulting `communicationUserId` on the Dataverse user/contact (the `communicationUserId` column added by task 005). This is the durable `communicationUserId ↔ Dataverse` mapping used for sender resolution and token re-issue.
    • **Server-side chat-token minting** — mint `chat`-scoped ACS access tokens (`GetToken(user, ["chat"])` / `CreateUserAndToken`) for participants, server-side, 1–24h validity (default 24h), with a refresh callback shape ready for a future live client. **Even internal Entra users get chat tokens minted here** — the Entra→ACS token exchange is VoIP-scope only, so Chat is one uniform server-minting path (design §8.2).

    This layer talks to ACS **only from the BFF**. NFR-04: no ACS SDK on any client and **no token reaches a browser in R1** — the BFF holds the minted tokens and acts as the participant on ACS's behalf (the live-client browser-token path is the next project). Blueprint: `Azure-Samples/communication-services-authentication-hero-csharp` (trusted-service token minting + identity mapping). Do NOT build thread/membership ops here — that is task 011.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF architect for the Communication subsystem, specializing in ACS (Azure Communication Services) server integration. Authority on `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/` and the ADR-028 auth plane. Fluent in ADR-028 (central `TokenCredential`, no `new` credential), ADR-045 (Communication channel seams), ADR-010 (DI minimalism via `CommunicationModule`), ADR-032 (Null-Object kill-switch), §10 BFF Hygiene, §11 Component Justification, and `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A server-side ACS identity service exists in `Services/Communication/Acs/` that (1) creates an ACS identity and persists `communicationUserId` on the Dataverse user/contact for any participant lacking one, and (2) mints `chat`-scoped ACS tokens (1–24h) for participants — uniformly for internal and (future) external identities. The central ACS `TokenCredential` is injected (ADR-028); no credential is `new`'d. No token or ACS admin capability reaches any client (NFR-04/NFR-05). Registered via `CommunicationModule` (ADR-010). Build clean; unit tests pass; publish-size delta + CVE + bff-extensions Placement Justification reported.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      The messaging channel needs an identity plane before any thread or message can exist. ACS's documented model is a **trusted service + thin clients**: the BFF creates identities, mints scoped tokens, and (task 011) mutates thread membership; clients never hold ACS admin capability. R1 goes further than the usual sample — because R1 has **no live client at all** (§8.5), the minted chat tokens stay server-side and the BFF acts as the participant; the browser-token path is deferred to the next-project live upgrade.

      Two ACS SDKs enter the BFF here: `Azure.Communication.Identity` (1.3.1) for `CreateUser`/`GetToken`, thin over `Azure.Core` (already present). Design §8.9: negligible publish-size delta — but measure it (NFR-01). Token scope is `chat` only; the Entra→ACS exchange is VoIP-scope, so uniform server-minting is the correct single path regardless of the exchange's preview status (design §8.2, re-check note §8.9).

      **§11 Component Justification (concrete cost-of-doing-nothing):** without a NEW `Acs/` identity service there is **no identity plane** — ACS cannot address a participant, so no thread can be created (011), no message can be sent (020/051), and no inbound event can be attributed to a Dataverse user. The failure mode is a named contract failure (FR-03 cannot be satisfied; 011/020/051 are blocked), not "future flexibility." This does not overlap any existing service: there is no `Azure.Communication.*` anywhere in the tree today (design §2). The identity concern cannot be folded into an existing auth service because it mints a *different* token type (ACS chat scope) against a *different* resource (ACS, not Entra/Graph) — extension of `GraphClientFactory`/`ManagedIdentityCredentialFactory` would leak ACS specifics into the Entra plane.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Channels/CommunicationChannelDispatcher.cs (ADR-045 seam surface — the dispatch this identity plane will eventually feed via 020/051)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Channels/EmailChannelSender.cs (the "thin adapter over an external transport" shape to mirror)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Models/ (add ACS identity/token result models here — e.g. AcsIdentityMapping, AcsChatToken)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/CommunicationModule.cs (register the ACS identity service + ACS client here, unconditional per ADR-032)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Auth/ManagedIdentityCredentialFactory.cs (central credential precedent — inject the ACS `TokenCredential`, do NOT `new` one)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/AiModule.cs (reference for how a central `TokenCredential` is resolved + passed to an Azure SDK client)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-03">BFF creates ACS identities, persists `communicationUserId` on the Dataverse user/contact, and mints `chat`-scoped tokens server-side for all participants. A participant without an ACS identity gets one created + mapped on first use.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-04">No ACS SDK on any client; NO token or ACS admin capability reaches any client in R1. The BFF holds minted tokens and acts as the participant.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-05">Inject the central ACS `TokenCredential` (ADR-028). MUST NOT `new` a `TokenCredential` / `ConfidentialClientApplication` / ACS connection-string credential inline; resolve it from DI.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Auth v2 — server-side token minting only; central credential; no `new` credential anywhere.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-045">The identity plane serves the messaging channel provider (020/051) that dispatches by `CommunicationType`; keep it channel-scoped and behind the Communication service boundary — do not leak ACS types outside `Services/Communication/`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Register the ACS identity service + ACS client via `CommunicationModule` only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032">Registration is unconditional (Null-Object if feature-gated); if a kill-switch is used, provide a Null-Object impl so endpoints/services that depend on it register unconditionally.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MUST NOT build thread/membership ops here (task 011) — identity + token minting only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Token scope is `chat` only, validity 1–24h (default 24h), with a refresh-callback shape; uniform minting for internal + (future) external identities.</constraint>
    <constraint source="§11">State the concrete FR-03 failure mode prevented by the new `Acs/` service (no identity plane → no thread/send/attribution) in the PR; verify by grep that no `Azure.Communication.*` exists pre-task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="§10">bff-extensions Placement Justification in the PR; publish-size delta (baseline ~45.30 MB post-R4); no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/messaging-communication-app-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/messaging-communication-app-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>projects/messaging-communication-app-r1/plan.md</file>
