      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-010-di-minimalism.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-032-bff-nullobject-kill-switch.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Central credential injection (ADR-028)" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Auth/ManagedIdentityCredentialFactory.cs">
        Resolve the Azure `TokenCredential` from DI and pass it to the ACS `CommunicationIdentityClient` constructor. Never `new` a credential inline. Mirror how `AiModule` wires a central credential into an Azure SDK client.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Thin adapter over an external transport" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Channels/EmailChannelSender.cs">
        Wrap the ACS SDK behind a Spaarke-owned interface + result models; keep ACS types from leaking outside `Services/Communication/`.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Unconditional Communication DI (ADR-010/032)" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/CommunicationModule.cs">
        Register the ACS identity service + client here; keep registration unconditional (Null-Object if gated).
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read `.claude/agent-memory/researcher/acs-chat-integration-2026-07-16.md` if present, plus design §8.1–8.2 + §8.9 and spec FR-03/NFR-04/NFR-05, to lock the trusted-service token-minting model + the uniform-minting rationale.</step>
    <step order="2">Grep the tree to confirm no `Azure.Communication.*` exists today (`grep -r "Azure.Communication" src/`) — records the §11 "no existing overlap" evidence. Read `CommunicationChannelDispatcher.cs` + `EmailChannelSender.cs` for the seam shape, `ManagedIdentityCredentialFactory.cs` + `AiModule.cs` for the central-credential pattern, and confirm task 005's `communicationUserId` column exists on the user/contact schema.</step>
    <step order="3">Add `Azure.Communication.Identity` (1.3.1) to `Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj`. Verify it resolves over the existing `Azure.Core`; report the restore result.</step>
    <step order="4">Define the identity abstraction in `Services/Communication/Acs/`: `IAcsIdentityService` (`EnsureIdentityAsync(participantRef)` → creates+maps if missing, returns `communicationUserId`; `MintChatTokenAsync(communicationUserId)` → `chat`-scoped token, 1–24h). Add result models (`AcsIdentityMapping`, `AcsChatToken`) under `Services/Communication/Models/`.</step>
    <step order="5">Implement `AcsIdentityService` wrapping `CommunicationIdentityClient` — constructed from the DI-injected central `TokenCredential` + ACS endpoint (ADR-028, NFR-05; no inline credential). `EnsureIdentityAsync`: look up existing `communicationUserId` on the Dataverse user/contact; if absent, `CreateUser`, persist the mapping via the canonical Dataverse interface, return it. `MintChatTokenAsync`: `GetToken(user, ["chat"])`; expose validity + a refresh-callback shape.</step>
    <step order="6">Wire the `communicationUserId` persistence through the canonical Dataverse client interface (no direct SDK); ensure the mapping is idempotent (a participant already mapped is not re-created).</step>
    <step order="7">Register `IAcsIdentityService` + the ACS identity client in `CommunicationModule` (ADR-010), unconditional (ADR-032 Null-Object if a kill-switch is introduced). Confirm no token/ACS type escapes `Services/Communication/` (grep the API layer).</step>
    <step order="8">Write unit tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/`: (a) `EnsureIdentityAsync` creates+maps when no mapping exists and is a no-op when one exists (idempotent); (b) `MintChatTokenAsync` requests only the `chat` scope; (c) the service is constructed from the injected credential (no `new` credential — assert via DI wiring / a fake credential); (d) no token is exposed on any client-facing DTO (NFR-04 — grep/assert the endpoint surface is untouched).</step>
    <step order="9">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ --filter Acs`; build clean, tests green.</step>
    <step order="9.1">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o c:/tmp/msg-010-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~45.30 MB baseline (NFR-01). `Azure.Communication.Identity` is thin over `Azure.Core` — expect a small delta; justify if ≥+5 MB.</step>
    <step order="9.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVE from the ACS package add.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` on the diff (focus: token never reaches a client, credential injected not `new`'d, ACS types don't leak the boundary); `adr-check` against `spec.md` (ADR-028 credential, NFR-04/05, ADR-010/032, §11 justification). Resolve Critical findings; cite bff-extensions Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (BFF hot-path — shared `Services/Communication/`; coordinate with email-r4 + notification-spine-r1).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (010 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (token validity chosen, mapping-persistence path, DI registration shape, publish-size delta).</step>
  </steps>

