  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`IAcsIdentityService` + `AcsIdentityService` exist in `Services/Communication/Acs/`; the only ACS SDK added is `Azure.Communication.Identity`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`EnsureIdentityAsync` creates an ACS identity + persists `communicationUserId` on the Dataverse user/contact when none exists, and is a no-op (returns the existing mapping) when one exists — idempotent.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`MintChatTokenAsync` mints a token with the `chat` scope only, validity 1–24h; a test asserts the scope.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The ACS client is constructed from the DI-injected central `TokenCredential`; no `new` credential / connection-string credential appears inline (ADR-028 / NFR-05).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No token or ACS admin capability is exposed on any client-facing DTO/endpoint (NFR-04 — grep/diff-verifiable); no client-side ACS SDK is added.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Service + client registered via `CommunicationModule`, unconditional (ADR-010/032); ACS types do not leak outside `Services/Communication/`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` clean; tests green; publish-size delta reported vs ~45.30 MB (small); no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Depends on 003 (ACS spike — proves identity+token+Event Grid round-trip and measures publish-size) and 005 (the `communicationUserId` column on user/contact). Blocks 011 (thread/membership ops need identities), 020 (sender), and 051 (outbound send uses the sender's minted token).

    Strict scope: identity + token minting ONLY. Thread create, participant add/remove, and retention config are task 011. If a step seems to require a `ChatThreadClient`, stop — that is 011's surface.

    Re-check before locking token design: the Entra→ACS *chat*-scope exchange is preview-gated to VoIP (design §8.9). Uniform server-minting works regardless, so this task is not blocked by that status — but note the finding in `current-task.md` for 011.

    Reference impl to copy: `Azure-Samples/communication-services-authentication-hero-csharp` — the BFF trusted-service token-minting + identity-mapping blueprint.
  </notes>

